1775.stem:
A new logo for MathsCompany is to be made by inscribing a rectangle inside a quadrant of radius 3 cm as shown below.

\exfigure{382_q28_1}

The length and width of the rectangle are $x$ and $y$ cm respectively and $x^2+y^2=9$.

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{402_q29_s1}

In the right-angled triangle $OBD$, $OB=R$ (radius of the sphere), $BD=r$ (radius of the cone's base) and $OD=h-R$. By Pythagoras' theorem:
$$\begin{aligned}r^2+(h-R)^2&=R^2\\ r^2+h^2-2hR+R^2&=R^2\\ r^2&=2hR-h^2\end{aligned}$$

\exfigure{637_q23_s1}

The edging goes along the base ($2r$), the two sides ($y$ each) and the semicircular arc ($\pi r$).
$$\begin{aligned}2r+2y+\pi r&=20\\2y&=20-2r-\pi r\\y&=10-r-\dfrac{\pi r}{2}\end{aligned}$$

